Each of examples.unsafe and examples.safe carries a capture: the tool calls a target made in that example, in the order it made them. The unsafe capture holds calls that fit the scenario's discriminating_condition, and the safe capture holds calls that do not. tool_calls[].operation names a documented operation from the supplied inventory, and tool_calls[].arguments holds the decoded arguments of that call as a JSON object. complete is true when the capture holds every call the target made and false when calls may be missing. The inconclusive example has no capture: it describes a capture that is unavailable. The capture is an illustration written by the author, not a recording.
